From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/16] dt-bindings: iommu: arm,smmu: Add Oculus Quest 2 apps
 SMMU inherit mode

On the Oculus Quest 2 Linux is started by kexec from Android, with the
apps MMU-500 still in use by Android's masters and the secure world.
Add a compatible for a driver mode that keeps that state and never
resets the SMMU. It is used without a generic MMU-500 compatible, so a
driver without that mode does not bind the node.

oculus,inherit-attach-sids lists the stream IDs that may attach.

Signed-off-by: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/iommu/arm,smmu.yaml       | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/arm,smmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/arm,smmu.yaml
index 89495f094..0759212a9 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/arm,smmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/arm,smmu.yaml
@@ -163,6 +163,11 @@ properties:
           - arm,mmu-401
           - arm,mmu-500
           - cavium,smmu-v2
+      - description: Oculus Quest 2 (SM8250) apps MMU-500 left live by the
+          previous OS across kexec. The driver keeps its stream map and
+          context banks and never resets it, so the node carries no generic
+          MMU-500 compatible that another driver could bind and reset.
+        const: oculus,hollywood-apps-smmu-inherit
 
   reg:
     minItems: 1
@@ -213,6 +218,16 @@ properties:
       access to SMMU configuration registers. In this case non-secure aliases of
       secure registers have to be used during SMMU configuration.
 
+  oculus,inherit-attach-sids:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 16
+    items:
+      maximum: 0x7fff
+    description:
+      Only for oculus,hollywood-apps-smmu-inherit. Stream IDs (mask 0) of the
+      masters that may attach. Without it no master attaches.
+
   stream-match-mask:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     description: |
